\section{Elapsed time between runs}

Teachers often care not only about \emph{what} a student ran, but also
about how long they paused before the next attempt.
The playback viewer only needs a lightweight approximation, so we use the
commit author date that [[begin_run]] records at run start.

That approximation is good enough for a quick \enquote{instant retry vs.
deliberate pause} signal, but it is still slightly noisy.
Interrupted runs may never record an end time, and playback works from Git
commit summaries rather than full run blocks.
The helper here therefore measures the interval from the previous displayed
student commit to the current one, while the ProgSnap2 analyser computes the
more precise end-to-start interval from the run data itself.

\subsection{Parsing ISO timestamps defensively}

The run logs and Git commit dates both use ISO timestamps.
We treat empty or malformed strings as missing data rather than raising, so
the viewer can simply omit the elapsed-time line when the underlying data is
incomplete.

<<commits functions>>=
def _parse_iso(value):
    """Return ``datetime.fromisoformat(value)`` or ``None``.

    Empty or invalid timestamps are treated as missing.
    """
    if not value:
        return None
    try:
        return datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(value)
    except ValueError:
        return None
