A review run is recognised by its subcommand, which makes the list of
review subcommands a piece of vocabulary that the recorder and this
reader must agree on: the recorder consults it to decide whether to
log an invocation at all (\cref{learnlog}), and disagreement would
mean runs that are recorded and then hidden, or filtered and never
written.
So [[REVIEW_SUBCOMMANDS]] is not defined here: it comes from
\cref{gitrepo} through the import above, exactly like
[[RUN_ID_FIELD]] and [[TRAILER_PREFIX]]---one definition that both
halves read is what makes disagreement impossible rather than merely
unlikely (\cref{sec:review-subcommands}).

Only the first two tokens decide.
Anything after them is options and arguments ([[learnlog list --all]]
is still a review run), and a bare [[learnlog]] with no subcommand is
not one---the recorder does not log it either.

<<commits functions>>=
def is_review_command(command):
    """Return true if ``command`` is a learnlog review run.

    Review runs are ``learnlog play``, ``learnlog list`` and
    ``learnlog metrics``: the subcommands with which a student
    looks back at their own history.
    """
    parts = command.split()
    return (
        len(parts) > 1
        and parts[0] == "learnlog"
        and parts[1] in REVIEW_SUBCOMMANDS
    )
@

The internal test is the difference between the two: learnlog's own
activity minus the part of it that belongs to the student.
Writing it as a difference rather than as a second list of subcommands
means a subcommand can never be both, and that a repository recorded by
an older version---which logged subcommands this list has never heard
of---still classifies every one of them as plumbing.

<<commits functions>>=
def is_internal_command(command):
    """Return true if ``command`` is learnlog's own plumbing.

    Learnlog activity that is not a review run: the ``pip``
    install performed by ``learnlog init``, and records of
    other subcommands left by versions that logged them.
    """
    return (
        is_learnlog_command(command)
        and not is_review_command(command)
    )
@

