\section{Filtering [[git show]] output}

We could fetch the raw commit message separately
([[git log --format=%B]]), but that would require an extra subprocess
call per commit.
Instead, we extract the message directly from the [[git show]]
output---it is indented with four spaces---rewrite it, and reconstruct
the output in place, reusing [[parse_show_sections]] to locate the
boundaries.

Two different rewrites need this: merging a run's trailer back into its
header (\cref{sec:run-join}) and dropping learnlog's internal runs
(review runs stay---\cref{sec:filter-learnlog}).
Taking the rewrite as a parameter keeps the fiddly
un-indent/re-indent surgery in one place instead of two.

<<commits functions>>=
def rewrite_show_message(show_output, rewrite):
    """Apply ``rewrite`` to the message inside ``git show`` output.

    ``rewrite`` maps the un-indented commit message to a new one.
    Returns the reconstructed output, or ``None`` when the
    rewritten message is empty.
    """
    lines = show_output.split("\n")
    header_end, diff_start = parse_show_sections(lines)

    <<extract and rewrite raw message>>
    <<reconstruct show output>>
@

<<extract and rewrite raw message>>=
end = diff_start if diff_start is not None else len(lines)
msg_lines = lines[header_end + 1:end]
raw_msg = "\n".join(
    line[4:] if line.startswith("    ") else line
    for line in msg_lines
)
new_msg = rewrite(raw_msg)

if not new_msg.strip():
    return None
@

<<reconstruct show output>>=
reindented = []
for line in new_msg.split("\n"):
    if line:
        reindented.append("    " + line)
    else:
        reindented.append("")

header = lines[:header_end + 1]
diff = lines[end:] if diff_start is not None else []
return "\n".join(header + reindented + diff)
@

<<commits functions>>=
def filter_show_output(show_output):
    """Filter learnlog's internal runs from ``git show``.

    Returns ``None`` if all run blocks were filtered out.
    """
    return rewrite_show_message(
        show_output, filter_internal_runs,
    )
@


\section{Retrieving commit detail}

Filtering is enabled by default because learnlog's plumbing is never
part of the student's story---a teacher reviewing the log should not
have to remember a flag to get a clean view.
The [[filter_internal]] parameter lets the [[--all]] flag disable it
for debugging or completeness.
Review runs come through either way: they are the student's activity,
not learnlog's, and hiding them behind a flag would hide the very
reflection the recorder logs them for.

The trailer map is a parameter rather than something we fetch here
because callers show many commits in a row: fetching it per commit
would read the whole log once per displayed run.
Callers that have no map---tests, and anyone who only wants the commit
as it was recorded---see the header alone, with no end time or captured
I/O.

<<commits functions>>=
def get_commit_detail(repo, commit_hash,
                      filter_internal=True,
                      trailers=None):
    """Return ``git show`` output for a single commit,
    reordered so the diff appears before the message.

    ``trailers`` is the map from :func:`get_run_trailers`; when
    given, each run's results are merged into its header block.
    When ``filter_internal`` is ``True`` (the default),
    learnlog's internal run blocks are stripped from the commit
    message; review runs are kept.  Returns ``None`` if every
    run in the commit was internal.
    """
    result = repo.git("show", commit_hash)
    detail = result.stdout

    if trailers:
        detail = rewrite_show_message(
            detail,
            lambda message: merge_run_trailers(
                message, trailers,
            ),
        )
    if filter_internal and detail is not None:
        detail = filter_show_output(detail)
    if detail is None:
        return None

    return reorder_commit_detail(detail)
@

Let's verify that a run's results show up in its header commit once
